==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGating  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_CareTeamGating.als
    rationale: Removing F_CareTeamGating lets the model find a world where a clinician with no care-team membership obtains a Permitted outcome on RecordLookup or AddNote, directly violating FR-004.
    expected to FAIL: FR_004_CareTeamGating, OwnershipBasedAccess
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCorrespondence  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditCorrespondence.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditCorrespondence allows the model to produce an Operation with an audit entry whose accessor differs from the operation's caller, and allows orphan audit entries, violating both always-on audit and attribution correctness.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit, AttributionCorrectness, FR_013_AuditEntryShape
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_AuditEntryShape: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Removing F_PermissionMatrix lets PermMatrix.Allowed become arbitrary, making it possible for HospitalAdministrator to have RecordLookup in the allowed set, breaking LeastPrivilege and PermissionCompleteness.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, PermissionCompleteness, PermissionGrounding, FR_017_AdminOnlyAuditEndpoint
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - PermissionCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - PermissionGrounding: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AdminOnlyAuditEndpoint: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyClinicalNotes  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AppendOnlyClinicalNotes.als
    rationale: Removing F_AppendOnlyClinicalNotes allows two distinct Permitted AddNote operations to link to the same ClinicalNote atom, simulating a 'reuse/overwrite' of a note entry that violates the append-only invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_011_NotesAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_NotesAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ClinicalEndpointsBlockAdmin  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_ClinicalEndpointsBlockAdmin.als
    rationale: Removing F_ClinicalEndpointsBlockAdmin allows a model world where a HospitalAdministrator caller obtains Permitted on AddNote, directly violating FR-005 administrator content-blindness.
    expected to FAIL: FR_005_AdminNoClinicalContent, LeastPrivilege
      - FR_005_AdminNoClinicalContent: PASS (vacuous?)
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_PermittedResponseIsSuccess  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_PermittedResponseIsSuccess.als
    rationale: Removing F_PermittedResponseIsSuccess allows the model to assign SuccessResponse to a Denied outcome, meaning both denied and permitted operations produce the same SuccessResponse — or inversely, Denied produces a distinct response shape that leaks existence of the resource.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_006_ByteEquivalentResponse
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_ByteEquivalentResponse: FAIL (expected)

